; print --display-amount EXPR leaves out each posting whose EXPR is zero
; (unless --empty is given), and EXPR may read the running total: `total`
; is the sum of the postings up to and including this one.  B brings the
; total back to $0, so print leaves B out; A, C and D are printed with
; their own amounts, D's although its running total is $8.  print
; computes running totals only when an option that can read them is
; given, as --display-amount and --amount can, since it never displays
; them itself.

2024/01/01 A
    (Budget:Food)    $-10

2024/01/02 B
    (Budget:Food)    $10

2024/01/03 C
    (Budget:Food)    $5

2024/01/04 D
    (Budget:Food)    $3

test print --display-amount total
2024/01/01 A
    (Budget:Food)                               $-10

2024/01/03 C
    (Budget:Food)                                 $5

2024/01/04 D
    (Budget:Food)                                 $3
end test
